Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: software adapter for Windows and macOS profiles

Under a Windows or macOS profile on a Linux host that renders through
ANGLE SwiftShader, navigator.gpu.requestAdapter() returns an adapter
backed by the bundled SwiftShader Vulkan driver. Chrome otherwise blocks
CPU adapters, so a page finds no WebGPU at all, which a Windows or Mac
Chrome with a real GPU does not show. Only the CPU-adapter block is
lifted, only for that verified SwiftShader device, and the driver loads
only from the browser's own directory, never from the system. Adapter
identity, limits and validation stay as SwiftShader reports them, and
other profiles and contexts keep the upstream behavior.

